              ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^2 \\,\\textrm d x.$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "We apply the power rule with $n=2$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int x^2 \\,\\textrm d x = \\dfrac{x^{2+1}}{2+1} + C = \\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\ &= {x}^{2}\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
